# A day over the tundra on seed 4, three minutes, to show how big the world is. It opens briefly high over the foothills in the morning,
# looking from the glacier range round to the plains, then comes down to fly low across the plateau, over the strait and up to the highest
# point on the far side while the day runs on, and turns back from the top to sweep slowly over the tundra it crossed as the sun sets and the aurora comes up.
# Format and compass in crates/ochre-gameplay/src/flythrough.rs. The render distance is about 16 km, more the higher it climbs.
# seconds   x       z        height  yaw  pitch  day
# high over the foothills in the morning light, the glacier range ahead in the north-west, then turning clockwise to the plains
0     10500  -21100  260   318    4   0.300
7     10490  -21090  310   370    3   0.308
14    10480  -21070  330   430    1   0.318
# down the foothills and out low over the plateau
25    11300  -20450  150   485   -4   0.326
36    12100  -19800    8   480   -1   0.330
# east over the plateau, the sun passing noon, then the strait and the ridge on the far side
56.9   13800  -18900     6   464    0   0.387
79.3   15800  -18400     6   460    0   0.449
99.2   17600  -18100     6   455    0   0.503
111.2  18700  -18000     6   450    0   0.536
124.2  19900  -18000    35   450    3   0.571
# along the ridge well above the ground, up to the highest point on the far side
128.6  20300  -17942   100   450    6   0.583
133.6  20700  -17885   120   452    8   0.597
137.0  20900  -17857   150   452    8   0.606
142.0  20950  -17850    60   450    4   0.620
# at the top it turns back to the west, and sweeps slowly left to right over the tundra it crossed, the sun setting at the right and the aurora coming up
151.0 20948  -17848    60   585    3   0.680
164.0 20948  -17848    60   634    3   0.745
173.0 20948  -17848    60   672    5   0.790
181.0 20948  -17848    60   700    8   0.830
